SUMMARY:The Ya-G’s
LOCATION:The Lilypad\, 1353 Cambridge St\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:$10+ suggested donation / 7:30 doors / 8pm show / seated & stan
 ding / all ages Behold the Ya-G's\, a band birthed during Covid by scruffy
  neighborhood dads deprived of live music and deciding to make their own. 
 They’re multi-instrumentalists\, but whatever they play\, from accordion
  to slide guitar\, it’s all about the song. Depending on where their fan
 cy leads them\, the set list might include Prince\, VU\, Waterboys\, Beatl
 es\, XTC\, Replacements\, Talking Heads\, Tarbox Ramblers\, Kinks\, and so
 me originals too —all with jangly rhythms and hoarse harmonies that’ll
  make you want to sing and stomp along.\nhttps://www.lilypadinman.com/home
 /2026/11/24/the-ya-gs\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://www.lilypadinman.com/home/2026/11/24/the-ya-gs
